window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>MEET DR KATE HANSON. SHE’S A FORENSIC PSYCHOLOGIST WHO GETS INTO THE MINDS OF THE WORST KILLERS IMAGINABLE.<br> <br> It’s 1:23 in the morning when Kate gets the call. News at this time is never good, but this call is one of the worst.<br> <br> A body has been found in a shallow grave on the outskirts of Birmingham. It’s badly decomposed, but forensic psychologist Kate Hanson is sure she knows who it is.<br> <br> Nineteen-year-old Elizabeth Williams disappeared a year ago. She was a good student who simply vanished off the face of the earth.<br> <br> The post-mortem doesn’t reveal a cause of death. Elizabeth was found naked, apart from a silk scarf around her neck. But she wasn’t strangled.<br> <br> Then another young woman is attacked out on a lonely road late at night. Same MO. Kate knows Elizabeth’s killer is still out there, and they’re not going to stop . . .<br> <br> The clock is ticking. Kate must find them before they kill again.</p>"; 
